  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/open-air-2025-argel-mdr/var/event_34772_1",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/open-air-2025-argel-mdr/var/ri-1.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Argel-MDR-1-Argel-Monte-de-Ramos-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/open-air-2025-argel-mdr/var/ri-1.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Open Air Performance Series: Argel MDR"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'><span style='font-size: 14pt;'><i>ARGEL MDR<br /> </i></span>Open Air Performance Series<i><br /> </i></span></b></span></span><b><i></i></b></h4> <div class='ewa-rteLine'> <div class='ewa-rteLine'> <div class='ewa-rteLine'> <div class='ewa-rteLine'> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>From&nbsp;<strong>July 7th – August 29th, 2025</strong>&nbsp;join us for a free, 1-hour performance <strong>every Monday to Friday at 6PM</strong> as part of our Open Air Performance Series. By expanding our arts experiences into Town Centre Park, we hope these events will excite our patrons and introduce us to new faces and Lake Lafarge lovers alike. Grab your picnic basket and enjoy a free professional concert in the park!</span></p> <p><i>The Evergreen Cultural Centre Society is supported by Port Coquitlam Community Foundation Theatre Society Legacy Fund.</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> </div> <div> <hr> </div> </div> <div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</span></strong></p> </div> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Argel MDR</strong> is a Filipino-Canadian singer-songwriter and musical theatre performer based in Surrey, Canada. Known for his soulful voice and emotional depth, Argel’s music blends heartfelt storytelling with influences from artists like Sam Smith, One Republic, and Original Pinoy Music (OPM). His single Sail Away was featured on several Spotify editorial playlists, including Fresh Finds Philippines, and earned him recognition as a rising artist. In 2021, he was nominated for Pop Artist of the Year and received the Excellence Award by a BIPOC Artist at the Fraser Valley Music Awards.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>A versatile performer, Argel has also made his mark in musical theatre. He played Horton the Elephant in <i>Seussical</i> (Align Entertainment), where his vocal ability and stage presence shone. In <i>Elf! The Musical</i> (Arts Club), he performed as Manager/Ensemble, earning an Ovation Award for Outstanding Performance for his standout work in the production. His theatre experience enhances his music, infusing it with a theatrical, emotionally charged energy that captivates live audiences.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Argel’s upcoming role as Joseph in <i>Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat</i> at Metro Theatre is another exciting chapter in his theatre career, showcasing his versatility as both a singer and actor. Beyond his artistry, Argel is a passionate advocate for diversity, inclusion, and anti-racism, using his platform to uplift the voices of immigrants and marginalized communities. With a powerful combination of music, theatre, and advocacy, Argel MDR continues to inspire and entertain, creating art that resonates with people from all walks of life.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><i>&#8220;With his emotive voice, dynamic performances, and commitment to meaningful social change, Argel MDR is a rising star in both the Filipino-Canadian music scene and the broader music landscape.&#8221;</i>&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span data-ccp-props='{}'>&nbsp;</span></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
