  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/ebony-roots/event_34645_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/ebony-roots/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ebony-roots-no-text.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g8348740"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/ebony-roots/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ebony Roots"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>EBONY ROOTS<br /></i></span></strong><strong><span style='color: #000000;'>Sound the Alarm</span></strong></h4> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><b>ABOUT THE SHOW<br /></b></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Ebony Roots is a concert celebration of African Descent/Black music &#8211; from 300 year old spirituals to Motown, and everything in between. It features a journey through Black music representing the evolving emancipation of the African-Descent community from the North American perspective. This powerful and intimate musical experience features prison/work songs, passionate spirituals, iconic songs from the stage, to the emergence of Black Soul, R&amp;B, Blues, and Motown.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This project was produced by Brandon Thornhill with support from Vancouver&#8217;s own award-winning company, Sound the Alarm: Music/Theatre (www.soundthealarm.ca) who is known for touring Music of the Night: The Concert Tour and A Whole New World.</span><b></b></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</span><br /></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Vocalist <strong>Brandon Thornhill</strong> serves as this concert’s lead curator, designer and producer. He initiated this project with the desire to advocate for his African Descent community, creating opportunities to highlight and celebrate Black music and artists in Canada and America. As producer, supported in mentorship and administration by Sound the Alarm: Music/Theatre, Brandon curated the repertoire as well as inviting the singers and artists involved. With a Masters Degree in Voice, and a vibrant career as a voice artist, and R&amp;B band vocalist, Brandon is a talented storyteller and helps blend the music and its historical significance into a wonderful program.</span></p> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults: $45 | Seniors: $41 | Students: $16</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
