  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-intro-to-improv-acting-2025/event_35065_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-intro-to-improv-acting-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/3.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-intro-to-improv-acting-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adult Intro to Improv &amp; Acting"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><strong><span style='color: #000000;'>ADULT INTRO TO IMPROV &amp; ACTING<br /></span></strong><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Educator Michael Charrois</span><br /></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Join Arts Educator, Michael Charrois, for an evening of improv &amp; acting. This fun, fast paced drama workshop for adults plays with the basics of spontaneous collaborative storytelling. We will play games for Character and Narrative and learn scenarios to hang the improvisation on. No memorization required, just a willingness to say &#8220;Yes!&#8221; and have fun. This workshop is suitable for all experience levels.<br /></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This fun, fast paced drama workshop for adults plays with the basics of spontaneous collaborative storytelling: Accepting (<em>Yes&#8230; let&#8217;s!</em>), Advancing (<em>Yes&#8230; and</em>) and Overcoming Obstacles (<em>Yes&#8230;but</em>) while working together to tell stories.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Improvisation is Life; it&#8217;s teamwork, collaboration, listening, communication, and the ability to adapt and problem-solve.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>And just like Life, if you accept, advance and overcome obstacles, there&#8217;s no telling where improvisation takes you, but if you block and say &#8220;No&#8221; the story goes nowhere. We will play games for Character and Narrative and learn scenarios to hang the improvisation on. No memorization required, just a willingness to say &#8220;Yes!&#8221; and have fun.</span></p> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION&nbsp;</strong></span></h4> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Tuesdays at 6:30PM | $85.00 per person<br />September 9 &#8211; 23, 2025<br /></span></h4> <hr> <h4>&nbsp;</h4> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR</strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><br /></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Michael Charrois is a professional actor (UBCP/Actra and Equity) with over 30 years of teaching experience. He currently teaches Drama classes for Evergreen Cultural Centre, Burnaby&#8217;s Shadbolt Centre Community Programs, and has taught Continuing Education classes for the Vancouver School Board.&nbsp;</span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
