  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-acting-character-development-2025/event_35066_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-acting-character-development-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/4.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-acting-character-development-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adult Improv &amp; Acting: Character Development"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><strong><span style='color: #000000;'>ADULT IMPROV &amp; ACTING: CHARACTER DEVELOPMENT<br /></span></strong><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Educator Michael Charrois</span><br /></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Arts Educator, Michael Charrois, invites you to an evening of improv and acting to develop foundational skills in character development. Learn about physicality, voice, personality traits, relationships, wants, and needs to fully inhabit characters and engage authentically with scenes. Experiment with posture, gestures, facial expressions, and movement to embody different characters physically, and explore contrasting objectives, conflicting desires, and unexpected alliances to create engaging and dynamic scenes. Inject genuine emotions and vulnerabilities into scenes to add authenticity, connection, and comedic contrast for more engaging and memorable performances.</span></p> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION <br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Tuesdays at 6:30PM | $85.00 per person<br /><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'>November 4 &#8211; 25, 2025 (No class November 11)</span></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><br /></span></h4> <p>&nbsp;</p> <hr> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span><span style='font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;'>Michael Charrois is a professional actor (UBCP/Actra and Equity) with over 30 years of teaching experience. He currently teaches Drama classes for the Evergreen, Burnaby&#8217;s Shadbolt Centre Community Programs and has taught Continuing Education classes for the Vancouver School Board.</span></h4> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM<br /></strong><strong><br /></strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
