  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/leslie-dala/event_34641_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/leslie-dala/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/IMG_1416.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g8873160"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/leslie-dala/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Leslie Dala: Romance to Radiohead"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>LESLIE DALA: ROMANCE TO RADIOHEAD</i></span></strong><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><br /></span></strong></h4> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><b>ABOUT THE SHOW<br /></b></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Always popular with audiences, Leslie Dala intimately narrates from the piano how the works of the greatest composers of the 19th, 20th and 21st centuries have personally inspired him.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><em>Romance to Radiohead</em> features music by Clara Schumann (3 Romances, Op.11), Franz Liszt (Petrarch Sonnets and Rigoletto Fantasy), a selection of Radiohead songs (transcribed by Christopher O&#8217;Riley) and the solo piano version of Gershwin&#8217;s iconic Rhapsody in Blue. &nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Spanning music over a period of almost 200 years, the music is linked and inspired by the virtuosic piano writing of the early 19th century composer/ performers like Clara Schumann and Liszt. The jazz idiom of George Gershwin and the alternative rock idiom of Radiohead are cleverly infused  by Leslie on this &#8220;classical&#8221; foundation. &nbsp;</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE ARTIST</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Leslie Dala </span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>is the Associate Conductor and Chorus Director of Vancouver Opera and Music Director of the Vancouver Bach Choir. He enjoys an extensive multifaceted career spanning the genres of opera, symphonic music, choral and contemporary works. On the podium, Leslie is known for his passionate, dynamic, and charismatic approach to music making. He has conducted in Europe, Asia, throughout Canada and recently made his debut at Carnegie Hall and Santa Fe Opera.</span><strong><br /></strong></p> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults: $43 | Seniors: $39 | Students: $16</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-11-16T15:00-7::00"
      }
    ],
