  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/nesting-opening-reception/event_35139_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/nesting-opening-reception/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Maya-Beaudry-Childhood-Home-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g8882340"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/nesting-opening-reception/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "&quot;Maya Beaudry: Nesting&quot; Tour &amp; Opening Reception"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='font-size: 14pt;'><em>MAYA BEAUDRY: NESTING</em>&nbsp;TOUR &amp; OPENING RECEPTION<br /> </span></span></strong><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'>Saturday, September 6 | 5:30PM &#8211; 7:30PM<br /> Free to attend, drop-ins welcome.<br /> </span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Join us for an exhibition tour with the artist Maya Beaudry, followed by an opening reception for <em>Nesting</em>. Light refreshments will be served. The event is free and wheelchair accessible.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE EXHIBITION&nbsp;</span></span></strong></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Maya Beaudry builds spaces that breathe. Through layered textiles, stitched architectures, and photographic, sculptural surfaces, she gives form to the emotional residues of place—homes lost, cities transformed, and bodies remembered. Her practice is rooted in the material language of cloth and the conceptual terrain of memory, navigating the threshold between the built and the felt. Drawing on the visual language of gentrified cities and vanishing spaces, her practice recalls what has been lost while imagining new forms of habitation—ones that honor slowness, decay, and renewal. In doing so, she transforms textiles into mnemonic architectures and offers viewers a place to dwell.</span></p> <p>Image: <span class='TextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>Maya Beaudry,&nbsp;</span></span><em><span class='TextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>Childhood Home</span></span></em><span class='TextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>, 2024</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>, d</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>igital pigment print on cotton</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>,&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>33 x 51 x 3 in.</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>Image courtesy of the artist and Towards Gallery. Photography by LF Documentation</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'>.</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW82150548 BCX0'> </span></span></p> <div class='et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_2  et_pb_text_align_center et_pb_bg_layout_light'> <div class='et_pb_text_inner'>&nbsp;</div> </div> "
      }
    ],
