  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/chiaroscuro-sitar-sarod/event_35174_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/chiaroscuro-sitar-sarod/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Indian-FIlm.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g9020900"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/chiaroscuro-sitar-sarod/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Chiaroscuro - Double-Bill Recitals on the Sitar &amp; Sarod"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='color: #000000;'><strong><span style='font-size: 14pt; color: #000000;'><i>CHIAROSCURO &#8211; DOUBLE-BILL RECITALS ON THE SITAR &amp; SAROD<br /></i></span></strong></span></span><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Indian Classical Music Society of Vancouver</span></strong><br /></span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Listen to rāgas unravel in a play of light and shade with some of the most reputed names in the world of Hindustānī classical music at <em>Chiaroscuro &#8211; Double-Bill Recitals of Sitar &amp; Sarod</em>!</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>The evening begins with the cerebral and emotive artistry of sarod maestro Arnab Chakrabarty, joined by the virtuosic tabla and jodi exponent Sukhvinder Singh ‘Pinky’.</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>In the second half, sitar doyen Budhaditya Mukherjee, revered worldwide for his extraordinary command of his instrument and evocative expositions, takes the stage along with his longtime collaborator Soumen Nandy, whose sensitive tabla accompaniment complements every shade of the performance.</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Two generations of instrument mastery, striking musical architecture, and profound creativity come together on one stage for this rare, one-of-a-kind experience.</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This program is presented by the Indian Classical Music Society of Vancouver, with generous funding from Canada Council for the Arts &amp; Vancouver Foundation’s LEVEL </span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>BIPOC Grant.</span></p> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE:</strong><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Tickets ranging from $25.00 &#8211; $50.00</span><br /></span></span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><em>This is a rental event organized by the Indian Classical Music Society of Vancouver.</em></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
