  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/kids-dedsign-architecture-wednesday-2025/var/event_35075_2",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/kids-dedsign-architecture-wednesday-2025/var/ri-2.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/olivia-oliver-design-S6-5uIf4LmI-unsplash-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/kids-dedsign-architecture-wednesday-2025/var/ri-2.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CANCELLED | Petit Architect: Kids Design &amp; Architecture"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='color: #ff0000;'>CANCELLED |</span> PETIT ARCHITECT: KIDS DESIGN &amp; ARCHITECTURE<i><br /></i></b></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Educator <span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Farnaz Haidari</strong></span></span><br /></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-size: 12pt; color: #ff0000;'>Unfortunately, this event has been cancelled.</span></p> <hr> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Begin a journey of architectural discovery with our engaging and creative hands-on classes designed for kids aged 7 to 12! Every week, young architects will explore the incredible worlds of famous architects and design concepts, growing their creativity through the creation of 2D drawings and 3D models.<span class='Apple-converted-space'>&nbsp;</span></span></p> <p class='p2'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>We transform learning into an exciting adventure, encouraging children to observe and appreciate their built and natural surroundings. As they learn about new concepts, their vocabulary blossoms and their fine motor skills thrive through the exciting process of drawing and model-making, just like real architects in the making!</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><b>SKILLS YOU&#8217;LL LEARN:</b></span></span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Intro to Architecture</strong>&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Students will get a glimpse into famous architectural styles, buildings, and architects. This will begin an appreciation for cultural history and the built environment all around us.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Advanced Spatial Awareness</strong>&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>By designing and building structures,&nbsp; students will learn to understand scale and perspective, enriching their spatial skills and grasp of geometry.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Strategic Problem-Solving</strong>&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Students will be encouraged to use their critical thinking skills by learning to anticipate challenges, adjust plans, and create innovative solutions.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Real World Understanding</strong>&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Through projects and discussions on building design and construction techniques, students will gain a tangible understanding of the concepts and processes involved in creating real-world structures centered around humans.&nbsp;</span></p> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION: <br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'>Ages 7 &#8211; 12 | $360 per person<br />Wednesdays at 4:30PM | September 24 &#8211; December 10, 2025</span></span></span></h4> <hr> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Farnaz Haidari</strong> is a creative Interior Designer with over ten years of experience in residential and commercial projects. With a diploma in Architectural Design and a passion for inspiring young minds, she joins the Petit Architect program as an educator.</span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Farnaz’s approach combines her design expertise with a love for creativity and mindful learning, empowering children to explore the world of design in engaging and imaginative ways. Outside of work, she enjoys Central Asian dance, meditation, and exploring local cafes.</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:&nbsp;</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM<br /></strong><strong><br /></strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
