  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/art-history-happy-hour-fall-2025/event_35256_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/art-history-happy-hour-fall-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/DSC_0029-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g9186960"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/art-history-happy-hour-fall-2025/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Art History Happy Hour"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 14pt;'><i>ART HISTORY HAPPY HOUR<br /></i></span><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Dr. Adrienne Fast</span></b></span></span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Let’s welcome back Adrienne Fast for another round of <strong><span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>Art</span> <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>History</span> Happy Hour</strong>! With her PhD in <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>Art</span> <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>History</span> and experience teaching a wide range of classes, Adrienne brings insight, stories, and a fresh perspective to every session. &nbsp;Join Dr. Fast is a series of fun and illuminating journeys through global <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>history</span> &#8211; enjoy a beverage, sit back and learn in this relaxed, entertaining format. Come for one class or all three! &nbsp;</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Join Adrienne Fast for a riveting evening of <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>history</span> and light beverages.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>October 7 | Hindu Temples<br /></span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This lively and engaging lecture introduces the fascinating world of Hinduism—complete with 330 million deities (don’t worry, you won’t be quizzed on them all). We’ll explore the beliefs and rituals that shape the religion, then take a virtual tour of Hindu temples, those epic stone masterpieces that are p<span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> spiritual haven, p<span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> architectural flex.</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>November 4 | Mesoamerican A<span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>rt</span> and H<span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>istory<br /></span></span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><span style='color: #ff0000;'>Cancelled | Unfortunately this session has been cancelled</span></strong></p> <p>Step into the colourful, complex, and occasionally terrifying world of Mesoamerican <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span>, where the Olmec, Maya, and Aztec civilizations turned stone, jade, and feathers into some of the most jaw-dropping creations in ancient <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>history</span>. This lecture serves up a wild mix of mythology, politics, and divine drama. Great for anyone who likes their <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>history</span> with a side of awe and a dash of dark humour. &nbsp;</span></p> <p class='elementToProof'><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>December 9 | The Ramayana, Visualized<br /><span style='color: #ff0000;'>Cancelled | Unfortunately this session has been cancelled</span></p> <p></span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>The Ramayana is unique in the world, yet there are countless different versions of it. The 25,000 verses of this epic poem recount the story of the Hindu god Ram, blending <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>history</span> and religion with poetry, adventure, and philosophy. This lecture will briefly outline of the story and then will go into detail with specific examples of how the Ramayana has been told through visual <span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span> in different eras and in different p<span class='outlook-search-highlight' data-markjs='true'>art</span>s of the world.</span></p> <hr> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION&nbsp;</strong></span></h4> <h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>$20 per person/class | Age 19+, wheelchair accessible.<br /></span></h4> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM<br /></strong><strong><br /></strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
