  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-character-development-spring-2026/event_35428_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-character-development-spring-2026/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/3.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/adult-improv-character-development-spring-2026/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adult Improv &amp; Acting: Character Development"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 12pt;'><span style='font-size: 14pt;'>ADULT IMPROV &amp; ACTING: CHARACTER DEVELOPMENT</span><br />with Michael Charrois</span><br /></b></span></span></h4> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This dynamic drama workshop for adults explores the fundamentals of narrative improvisation through collaborative storytelling techniques like accepting, advancing, and overcoming obstacles. Participants will build essential life and performance skills such as teamwork, communication, adaptability, and problem-solving. Led by arts educator Michael Charrois, the workshop includes fun games and exercises to develop characters and narratives without the need for memorization. Students will explore physicality, voice, personality traits, and relationships to bring authentic characters to life. Scenes will incorporate emotional depth, vulnerability, and comedic contrast to enhance audience connection and engagement. The course focuses on narrative improv—a form of spontaneous, longer-form storytelling that blends humor and emotion for rich, memorable performances.</span></p> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Arts Educator Michael Charrois invites you to an evening of improv and acting designed to deepen your foundational skills in character development. Building on concepts introduced in the previous session, this workshop will reinforce and expand your understanding through continued practice and new exercises.</span></p> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Explore physicality, voice, personality traits, relationships, wants, and needs to fully inhabit characters and engage authentically with scenes. You&#8217;ll experiment with posture, gestures, facial expressions, and movement to embody characters physically, while also diving into contrasting objectives, conflicting desires, and unexpected alliances to create dynamic, engaging interactions. By bringing genuine emotion and vulnerability into your performance, you&#8217;ll enhance authenticity, connection, and comedic contrast—resulting in more memorable, impactful scenes.</span></p> <p class='p1'><strong style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'>CLASS INFORMATION&nbsp;</p> <p></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Tuesday Evenings, March 3, &#8211; 17 | 6:30 &#8211; 8:30PM<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>$85/person<br />Age 18+</span></p> <hr> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR</p> <p></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Michael Charrois is a professional actor (UBCP/Actra and Equity) with over 30 years of teaching experience. He currently teaches Drama classes for the Evergreen, Burnaby&#8217;s Shadbolt Centre Community Programs and has taught Continuing Education classes for the Vancouver School Board.</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
