  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/hot-chocolate-nights-2025/var/event_35392_3",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/hot-chocolate-nights-2025/var/ri-3.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Hot-chocolate-nights-graphic_3-scaled.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g10201700"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/hot-chocolate-nights-2025/var/ri-3.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Hot Chocolate Nights"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><span style='font-size: 14pt;'><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;'>HOT CHOCOLATE NIGHTS</span></strong></span><br /><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>at the Art Gallery at Evergreen</span></strong></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Our fan-favourite Hot Chocolate Nights are back! Join us for a visit to the Art Gallery at Evergreen’s exhibition <em>Sharni Pootoogook: Creatures, Shadows, and Dreams</em> followed by a warm cup of hot chocolate to-go to kick off your Lights at Lafarge visit!</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE EXHIBITION</span></strong></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span class='TextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>The life and work of Sharni Pootoogook (1922–2003), though still largely un</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>der</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>explored, draws clear and fundamental connections between first-generation artists in&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed SCXW140979673 BCX0'>Kinngait</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>,</span></span><span class='TextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;</span></span><span class='TextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0' lang='EN-CA' xml:lang='EN-CA' data-contrast='auto'><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>Nunavut</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>,</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;and the current trends in Inuit graphic art. Her bold designs helped to shape and inform the course of Inuit printmaking during a period of great turmoil that threatened Inuit land,&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>culture</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;and traditional language</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>s</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>. Drawn from the Kelowna Art Gallery</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>’</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>s&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>p</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>ermanent&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>c</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>ollection and supplemented by works&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>on loan</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>from Simon Fraser University</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>, Burnaby</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>, this exhibition features works on paper that&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>demonstrate</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;Pootoogook</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>’</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>s trademark style of heavy linework and well-balanced design. Blurring the b</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>oundaries</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>&nbsp;between human and animal, the spiritual and the&nbsp;</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>physical</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>, Pootoogook</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>’</span><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW140979673 BCX0'>s work creates space for wonder and uncertainty.</span></span><span class='EOP SCXW140979673 BCX0' data-ccp-props='{}'>&nbsp;</span></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
