      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 18.6667px;'>ADULT CERAMICS: WHAT WE MAKE OF IT<br /></span><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>with Educator Julie Epp</span></b></span></span></h4> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Get inspired by the contemporary art on view at the Art Gallery at Evergreen and explore the endless possibilities of clay with artist Julie Epp. Begin with a guided tour and in-depth exploration of the exhibition, where you’ll reflect on its themes, emotions, and artistic practices. Then, return to the studio to create your own expressive ceramic artwork using hand-building techniques.</span></p> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Guided by Julie’s creative and reflective approach, participants will experiment with form, texture, and imagination while learning foundational clay techniques. Discover how clay can be both expressive and functional, shaped by your ideas and the stories you want to tell. Come ready to play, learn, and create something uniquely your own!</span></p> <p><strong style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'>CLASS INFORMATION&nbsp;</p> <p></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>5 Sessions to Choose From!&nbsp; |&nbsp; 6:30 &#8211; 9:30PM<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>$55/person per session<br />Age 18+<br /></span></p> <hr> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><br />ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span></p> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span class='s1'>J</span>ulie is a visual artist who works in painting, sculpture, and mixed media to explore themes of beauty, nature, and the human experience. Julie Epp is an award-winning artist from Abbotsford, BC and holds a BFA from the University of the Fraser Valley. She has exhibited throughout BC and teaches art to children and adults throughout the lower mainland.<br /></span>|<br /><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
