      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g10608780"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/burning-mom/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Burning Mom"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>BURNING MOM<br /></i><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>An Arts Club Theatre Company Production</span><br /></span></strong><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><span style='font-size: 12pt;'><i></i>By Mieko Ouchi</span><br /></span></strong></h4> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE SHOW<br /></span></strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>In this inspiring comedy, Dorothy realizes that life is too short to delay your aspirations. After losing her husband, she decides to take their RV on the road trip of his retirement dreams: she’s going to Burning Man. After all, it’s only a 21-hour drive to a weeklong culture festival and party with no plumbing in the middle of a desert—how hard can it be?</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><i>Burning Mom </i>is a stirring odyssey of self-discovery and tale of how art, everlasting roads, and human connection propel her along the way. You&#8217;ll laugh and cry as Dorothy&#8217;s story, based on the playwright&#8217;s mother&#8217;s life, invites you to take risks and enjoy the small moments in life—come along for the ride!</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ACCOMPANING PUBLIC PROGRAMS</span></strong><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Tasting Tuesdays</strong> | Tuesday, January 27&nbsp; (6 &#8211; 7:30PM)</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Enhance your theatre experience with Tasting Tuesdays! Enjoy a free tasting from a local brewery before the show.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Post-Show Talkback</strong> | Thursday, January 29&nbsp;</span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Stay in your seats for a post-show talkback with the creative team immediately following the performance.</span></p> <p class='p1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><span style='font-size: 10pt; color: #808080;'>Image: Susinn McFarlen in <em>Burning Mom</em>, 2025; set design by Patrick Rizzotti; costume design by Kirsten McGhie; lighting design by John Webber; projection design by Kim Clegg; photo by Moonrider Productions for the Arts Club Theatre Company.</span></p> <p></span></p> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults: $54 | Seniors: $46 | Students: $16 | Row A: $29</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
