  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/the-trollsons/var/event_34683_1",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/the-trollsons/var/ri-1.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/trollsons.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g10739820"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/the-trollsons/var/ri-1.l-L1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Spring Break: The Trollsons"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;'><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>THE TROLLSONS<br /></i><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>Presented by Pangaea Arts<i><br /></i>Part of our 2026 Spring Break Programming!</span></span></strong></span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE SHOW</span></strong></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Come deep into a fantastical forest as four masked characters and a live musician bring to life the folklore of Scandinavian trolls. It&#8217;s Grandpa Trollson&#8217;s 200th birthday party, but he refuses to come out of his tree stump to celebrate! But with the help of the audience, Grandpa cannot resist the power of storytelling. Join us for three truly interactive tales based on stories by Hans Christian Andersen, featuring live music, incredible masks, physical comedy, improvisation, and good old-fashioned troll trouble!</span></p> <p><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</span></strong></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>The Trollsons</strong> are a delightful family of masked trolls that have been performing together since 1995, and have been seen at festivals, special events, schools, theatres and Children’s Festivals throughout the world. They have a wide range of performances, including children’s theatre, festival-stage shows, and interactive roving characters. The incredible troll masks were made by award winning mask designer Melody Anderson.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Pangaea Arts</strong> is an award-winning intercultural, interdisciplinary world arts organization, formed to promote cultural interaction and the exchange of ideas between diverse communities and to introduce Canadian audiences to performance traditions from around world. As well as producing stunning world theatre collaborations, Pangaea Arts has brought a wide range of Theatre for Young Audiences productions to festivals, schools and communities since 1998.</span><b></b></p> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults &amp; Seniors: $24 | Students: $16</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
