  {
    "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/scene-study-march-2026/event_35644_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/scene-study-march-2026/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/5.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g11010340"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://evergreenculturalcentre.ca/events/scene-study-march-2026/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Scene Study: From Actor Choice to Directing Shape"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h2><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><strong><span style='font-size: 18.6667px;'>SCENE STUDY: FROM ACTOR CHOICE TO DIRECTING SHAPE<br /></span><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>Masterclass in Advanced Rehearsal Practice</span></strong><b><br /></b></span></span></h2> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Step inside the rehearsal room and experience how a scene transforms from first impulse to fully realized performance. </span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>This immersive masterclass for adult students reveals the craft behind compelling scene work, beginning with Stanislavski’s action-based approach and the essential question of what a character wants. From there, the process expands into purposeful directing that shapes space, rhythm, and focus, illuminating how individual choices evolve into powerful, cohesive storytelling. Participants move through a dynamic progression of action before text, relationship through staging, action applied directly to script, and thoughtful director-led refinement, running scenes multiple times so growth and transformation are clearly visible.<br /></span> <br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Perfect for emerging actors and anyone serious about deepening their understanding of performance and the collaborative rehearsal process.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Led by Vjosa Mala, an experienced actor and Performing Arts Educator with a Master of Arts in Applied Theatre from the University of Victoria, this workshop combines professional training with practical insight. Ideal for actors ready to deepen their craft and anyone passionate about&nbsp;performance,&nbsp;it offers rare access to the collaborative process that brings a script vividly to life.&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION | ONE NIGHT ONLY<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Tuesday, March 24 | 6 &#8211; 9PM<br /></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'>Age 18+ | $20, pay-more-if-you-can</span></span></p> <hr> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><br />ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR</p> <p></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'>Vjosa Mala</span></strong> is an actress, drama teacher, and an applied theatre practitioner. She studied Acting at University of Pristina- Kosovo. She also graduated with a Master’s Degree of Applied Theatre at University of Victoria- Canada. Her experience on working with children and youth took place in theatres, community centres, and schools in Europe and Canada. By working with children and youth, she had many opportunities to direct several theatre performances. Her teaching approach is based mostly on devised theatre, when she works without a pre-existing script wherein the participants can create and perform together. She also believes that theatre can be used as a tool for social purposes such as: social justice, community building, and education.</span> </p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
