      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><strong><span style='color: #000000;'><i>LAS MUJERONAS &#8211; A FLAMENCO SHOWCASE<br /></i>Jhoely Triana <br /></span></strong></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE SHOW<br />Las Mujeronas</strong> <em>[loss moo-hair-OWN-us]</em> is a powerful, trailblazing work that celebrates fierce and confident women navigating struggles, rebuilding their lives, and reclaiming their voices, identities, dreams, and passions. This performance features Flamenco Latinas in Canada as they explore immigrant identities and reconnect with their home cultures through the art of flamenco.</span></p> <div class='ewa-rteLine'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Incorporating flamenco elements such as Ida y Vuelta <em>[EE-da ee voo-EL-ta]</em> (“going and coming”)—a musical form influenced by the cultural exchange between the Americas and Spain—Las Mujeronas examines how migration shapes personal and collective narratives. The piece blends flamenco dance, poetry, singing, and storytelling to create a vibrant, emotional experience.</span></div> <div class='ewa-rteLine'>&nbsp;</div> <div class='ewa-rteLine'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>The performance culminates in a lively, interactive rumba flamenca, where the audience is invited to join in a follow-the-leader-style song and community dance party.</span></div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW45868553 BCX0'>Artistic Director/Choreographer:&nbsp;</span></strong><span class='NormalTextRun SCXW45868553 BCX0'>Johely Triana<br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Singer:</strong>&nbsp;Maria Avila&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Guitarist and Composer:</strong>&nbsp;Peter Mole&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Percussionist:</strong>&nbsp;Davide Sampaolo&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;' data-contrast='auto'><strong>Dancers:</strong> Rosa Celis, Marcela Lopez, Desiree Carlson Sanroman, Luiza Libardi, and Jessica Oryall.&nbsp; All of these dancers have completed the Professional Development Program from Flamenco Rosario</span></p> </div> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>ABOUT THE ARTISTS<br /></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>Jhoely Triana</strong> is a Colombian-born flamenco dancer and choreographer based in Vancouver. With a diverse dance background, Jhoely trained at the Goh Ballet Academy, earned a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Contemporary Dance from Simon Fraser University, and honed her flamenco skills at Al Mozaico Flamenco and Flamenco Rosario.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Her work has been showcased at renowned events such as the Victoria Flamenco Festival, Vancouver International Flamenco Festival, Vines Festival, New Works Dance, and the Vancouver Fringe Festival, among others. Jhoely&#8217;s choreography has also been featured at venues including The Dance Centre, Evergreen Cultural Centre, Knox Performance Centre, and during BC Culture Days.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>After spending three months training in Spain, Jhoely returns with a renewed sense of passion and authenticity in her art. Her performances are marked by a deep connection to the audience, where vulnerability and emotional authenticity take center stage, creating an immersive and resonant experience.&nbsp;</span></p> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <hr> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>SINGLE TICKETS ON SALE!</strong><br /></span></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Adults &amp; Seniors: $25 | Students: $16</span></p> <p><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong>BOX OFFICE: 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
