    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 14pt;'>ACTING FOR MUSICAL THEATRE &#8211; SENIOR<br /></span><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>Evergreen X Theatrix | with Arts Educator Morgan Misic</span></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Step beyond memorizing lines and into the craft of performance. <em>Acting for Musical Theatre</em> focuses on developing technique, presence, and authentic storytelling. Students will work on connecting truthful emotion to text and song, using movement, voice, and intention to bring characters to life. Through focused exercises and short scene work, they’ll explore how to analyze scripts, make clear acting choices, and communicate truthfully on stage.<br /></span><br /><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Each class builds the foundation for confident, expressive performances that strengthen every audition, role, and rehearsal experience.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION</p> <p></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Age 14 &#8211; 17<br />Tuesday Evenings, April 7 &#8211; June 9 | 6 &#8211; 7:30PM<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>$285/person | Save $35 when you bundle 2 or more Musical Theatre Academy classes!</p> <p><span style='text-decoration: underline;'><strong>Showcase: Wednesday, June 17</strong></span></span></p> <hr> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><br />ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span></p> <p><span class='s1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Morgan Misic’s passion for acting is undoubtedly her greatest asset. She started her career in Surrey at the young age of ten working as a background performer on multiple movies. She’s had numerous opportunities working with industry professionals thanks to graduating from Capilano University’s Acting for Stage and Screen Program. She has pursued her acting education in New York City studying at the Neighbourhood School of the Theatre, and later founded her own independent theatre company, “Quand Même,” where she produced, directed, and performed. </p> <p>While she continues to audition and perform whenever her busy schedule allows, Morgan is eager to share her knowledge with the next generation of performers and hopes to inspire them to pursue their own dreams in the arts.</span></p> <p></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
