    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h4><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='color: #000000;'><b><span style='font-size: 14pt;'>VOICE FOR MUSICAL THEATRE &#8211; JUNIOR<br /></span><span style='font-size: 12pt;'>Evergreen X Theatrix | with Arts Educator Sanders Whiting</span></b></span></span></h4> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;'>Sing with confidence, control, and expression. <em>Voice for Musical Theatre</em> develops the technical and artistic skills needed for healthy, dynamic singing on stage. Students will strengthen breath support, tone, and diction while learning how to use their voices safely across different musical styles. Each class focuses on connecting emotion to lyrics, improving vocal stamina, and building awareness of how the voice works. It’s a supportive, skill-focused environment that helps singers grow in both ability and confidence, preparing them for solos, ensembles, and auditions.</span></p> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong>CLASS INFORMATION</p> <p></strong></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Age 10 &#8211; 13<br />Saturday Mornings, April 11 &#8211; June 13 | 11AM &#8211; 12:30PM<br /></span><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>$285/person | Save $35 when you bundle 2 or more Musical Theatre Academy classes!</p> <p><span style='text-decoration: underline;'><strong>Showcase: Wednesday, June 17</strong></span></span></p> <hr> <p><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'><strong><br />ABOUT OUR EDUCATOR<br /></strong></span></p> <p><span class='s1'><span style='font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;'>Sanders Whiting is a veteran teacher and performer with degrees including an MFA in Theatre, a B.Music, and a B.Ed, and is a certified instructor of the Estill Voice Training model. He has worked in professional theatres across Canada, performing in shows such as&nbsp;<i>Lord of the Rings</i>,&nbsp;<i>Fiddler on the Roof</i>,&nbsp;<i>Sweeney Todd</i>, and most recently as Grandpa Joe in&nbsp;<i>Charlie and the Chocolate Factory</i>.&nbsp; He has been nominated for local Jessie and Ovation awards 4 times winning once for Forever Plaid.&nbsp; Sanders taught singing, voice, and speech in the professional theatre program at Capilano University for seven years, maintains a private singing studio, and currently serves as the Voice and Presentation Skills consultant for faculty at Simon Fraser University.</span></p> <p></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;'><span style='font-size: 16px;'><strong>REGISTER ONLINE OR AT THE BOX OFFICE:</strong><br /></span></span><span style='color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;'><strong> 604.927.6555 | Open Monday – Saturday, 12 – 5PM</strong></span></p> <p><!-- wp:pattern {'slug':'ajde_events/blocks'} /--></p> "
      }
    ],
